{
  "id": 503280198,
  "iid": 25649,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "atalk: Add support for ADSP packets",
  "description": "Extends the AppleTalk dissector to include support for AppleTalk Data Stream Protocol (ADSP). I've been using this pretty heavily to develop an ADSP implementation over in my project [TailTalk](https://github.com/FeralFirmware/TailTalk) to verify I'm generating packets as expected. I've also taken a capture of a real Mac OS 9 \\< - \\> Apple Printer transmission and attached it here for verifiation:\n\n[powerbook_print.pcap](/uploads/6b73b82f1af3098e1bf53880a92c1656/powerbook_print.pcap)\n\nIt appears to decode everything correctly from what I can see:\n\n![Scherm­afbeelding 2026-07-03 om 8.59.35 PM.png](/uploads/5eb2561541f5ffff5e0660596c6d03b0/Scherm_afbeelding_2026-07-03_om_8.59.35_PM.png){width=\"900\" height=\"500\"}\n\nADSP is somewhat TCP adjacent so we are missing equivalents like sequence number checks and such that Wireshark offers for TCP, but I figure this protocol is so niche we can add it at a later time :)\n\nMy first time contributing to Wireshark so I hope the changes aren't too far off. Thanks!",
  "state": "merged",
